[38;5;231m⏺[39m I'm treating this as a bounded change. The page and its rendering code already exist, so I'll ask a few questions,
  give you a short design here in chat, and wait for your yes before I edit anything. There won't be a spec file. Tell
  me if you'd rather have the heavier process.

  Where the filter goes on the page is easier to judge by looking, so I've opened a browser tab with three wireframes:

  [94m]8;id=sb3scb;http://localhost:56264/?key=cbd66924eabc331667468abbdd51a40a7cdf39efd01a676e0dd1472f338455fd\http://localhost:56264/?key=cbd66924eabc331667468abbdd51a40a7cdf39efd01a676e0dd1472f338455fd[39m]8;;\

  (It uses a lot of tokens, so say so if you'd rather keep this in the terminal.)

  - [1mA:[0m An "Event type" select on its own row between the intro text and the table, with a live count next to it
    ("Showing 8 of 48 events").
  - [1mB:[0m The same select to the right of the "Account activity" heading, with the count below the intro. It saves a row,
    but it gets cramped on narrow screens.
  - [1mC:[0m Same as A, plus a "Show failed sign-ins" button that sets the select to that type in one click. It's aimed at the
    support tickets, but it's one more control to build and review.

  I'd go with A. It matches the label-above-control rule in the guidelines and leaves room for a second filter later. C
  is worth it if the failed sign-in case matters enough to get its own button.

  Click one in the tab if you like, then reply here.

  The mockups are stored in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m, which is untracked and not in a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet. You may want to add
  [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m to [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m so it doesn't end up in a commit. I haven't changed that file.

